---
import SeoArticle from "../../components/SeoArticle.astro";
import { WORDS_PER_MINUTE } from "../../lib/text/measure";
import { faq } from "./faq";
---

<SeoArticle idPrefix="wc-seo" {faq}>
  <section aria-labelledby="wc-seo-counting">
    <h2 id="wc-seo-counting" class="sd-text-title">
      How we count words and characters
    </h2>
    <p>
      Characters are easy. Every letter, space, punctuation mark and even emoji
      count in the total.
    </p>
    <p>
      Words on the other hand are a little harder. We count a word as any group
      of letters or numbers between spaces. Hyphenated words count as one. Other
      dashes, double hyphens, and ellipses break up words.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="wc-seo-speaking">
    <h2 id="wc-seo-speaking" class="sd-text-title">
      Speaking time is an estimated
    </h2>
    <p>
      Speaking time takes into consideration your word count along with a
      common, steady speaking speed of {WORDS_PER_MINUTE} words per minute. It's helpful
      for estimating talks, voiceovers, and scripts. Dramatic reading may take longer,
      and conversational reading may take less.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="wc-seo-limits">
    <h2 id="wc-seo-limits" class="sd-text-title">Setting a limit</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        At most: stay below a max count, such as 650 words for a college essay
        or 280 characters for an X post.
      </li>
      <li>At least: reach a minimum.</li>
      <li>
        Exactly: hit a specific number, like how a six-word story or a 100-word
        drabble requires.
      </li>
      <li>
        Around: hit a number with some leeway when the precise number matters
        less, like a 300-word query letter or a one-minute script.
      </li>
      <li>Between: keep inside a range, like 250 to 650 words.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each format is a shortcut to filling in the settings for you: fiction from
      six-word stories to short stories, query letters, synopses and loglines,
      the Common App essay, posts on X, Bluesky and Threads, and spoken scripts
      from 30 seconds to five minutes. If you go over, we'll show you by how
      much to help you iterate on your text.
    </p>
  </section>
</SeoArticle>
